 991:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****     This subsection provides a set of functions allowing to manage the UART asynchronous
 992:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****     and Half duplex data transfers.
 993:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c **** 
 994:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****     (#) There are two modes of transfer:
 995:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****        (++) Blocking mode: The communication is performed in polling mode.
 996:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****             The HAL status of all data processing is returned by the same function
 997:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****             after finishing transfer.
 998:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****        (++) Non-Blocking mode: The communication is performed using Interrupts
 999:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****             or DMA, These API's return the HAL status.
1000:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****             The end of the data processing will be indicated through the
1001:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****             dedicated UART IRQ when using Interrupt mode or the DMA IRQ when
ARM GAS  /var/folders/d7/pb3dkhys6j3db_qtp_8v34p80000gn/T//ccF6Pqlc.s 			page 19


1002:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****             using DMA mode.
1003:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****             The HAL_UART_TxCpltCallback(), HAL_UART_RxCpltCallback() user callbacks
1004:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****             will be executed respectively at the end of the transmit or Receive process
1005:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****             The HAL_UART_ErrorCallback()user callback will be executed when a communication error i
1006:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c **** 
1007:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****     (#) Blocking mode API's are :
1008:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****         (++) HAL_UART_Transmit()
1009:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****         (++) HAL_UART_Receive()
1010:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c **** 
1011:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****     (#) Non-Blocking mode API's with Interrupt are :
1012:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****         (++) HAL_UART_Transmit_IT()
1013:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****         (++) HAL_UART_Receive_IT()
1014:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****         (++) HAL_UART_IRQHandler()
1015:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c **** 
1016:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****     (#) Non-Blocking mode API's with DMA are :
1017:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****         (++) HAL_UART_Transmit_DMA()
1018:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****         (++) HAL_UART_Receive_DMA()
1019:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****         (++) HAL_UART_DMAPause()
1020:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****         (++) HAL_UART_DMAResume()
1021:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****         (++) HAL_UART_DMAStop()
1022:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c **** 
1023:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****     (#) A set of Transfer Complete Callbacks are provided in Non_Blocking mode:
1024:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****         (++) HAL_UART_TxHalfCpltCallback()
1025:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****         (++) HAL_UART_TxCpltCallback()
1026:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****         (++) HAL_UART_RxHalfCpltCallback()
1027:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****         (++) HAL_UART_RxCpltCallback()
1028:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****         (++) HAL_UART_ErrorCallback()
1029:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c **** 
1030:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****     (#) Non-Blocking mode transfers could be aborted using Abort API's :
1031:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****         (++) HAL_UART_Abort()
1032:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****         (++) HAL_UART_AbortTransmit()
1033:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****         (++) HAL_UART_AbortReceive()
1034:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****         (++) HAL_UART_Abort_IT()
1035:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****         (++) HAL_UART_AbortTransmit_IT()
1036:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****         (++) HAL_UART_AbortReceive_IT()
1037:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c **** 
1038:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****     (#) For Abort services based on interrupts (HAL_UART_Abortxxx_IT), a set of Abort Complete Call
1039:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****         (++) HAL_UART_AbortCpltCallback()
1040:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****         (++) HAL_UART_AbortTransmitCpltCallback()
1041:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****         (++) HAL_UART_AbortReceiveCpltCallback()
1042:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c **** 
1043:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****     (#) A Rx Event Reception Callback (Rx event notification) is available for Non_Blocking modes o
1044:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****         reception services:
1045:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****         (++) HAL_UARTEx_RxEventCallback()
1046:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c **** 
1047:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****     (#) Wakeup from Stop mode Callback:
1048:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****         (++) HAL_UARTEx_WakeupCallback()
1049:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c **** 
1050:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****     (#) In Non-Blocking mode transfers, possible errors are split into 2 categories.
1051:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****         Errors are handled as follows :
1052:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****        (++) Error is considered as Recoverable and non blocking : Transfer could go till end, but e
1053:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****             to be evaluated by user : this concerns Frame Error, Parity Error or Noise Error
1054:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****             in Interrupt mode reception .
1055:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****             Received character is then retrieved and stored in Rx buffer, Error code is set to allo
1056:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****             to identify error type, and HAL_UART_ErrorCallback() user callback is executed.
1057:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****             Transfer is kept ongoing on UART side.
1058:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****             If user wants to abort it, Abort services should be called by user.
ARM GAS  /var/folders/d7/pb3dkhys6j3db_qtp_8v34p80000gn/T//ccF6Pqlc.s 			page 20


1059:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****        (++) Error is considered as Blocking : Transfer could not be completed properly and is abort
1060:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****             This concerns Overrun Error In Interrupt mode reception and all errors in DMA mode.
1061:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****             Error code is set to allow user to identify error type, and HAL_UART_ErrorCallback()
1062:Drivers/STM32L0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l0xx_hal_uart.c ****             user callback is executed.
